            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0530" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6354/352: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-10T23:00:00+02:00">April 10, 1942—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 10—6:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1766. Embassy’s 1746, April 10.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Spoke to Campbell at end of International Tin Committee meeting today. He
                        tells me Committee voted (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) that it was
                        prepared to recommend renewal of agreement to interested Government subject
                        to reservations of Bolivian Government outlined in section 3 of <pb
                            facs="0531" n="519" xml:id="pg519"/> number 1746; and (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">b</hi>) unanimously recommended liquidation of
                        buffer stock funds amounting to about 2½ million sterling by repayment of
                        money in proportion to respective contributions with exception of Siam which
                        will go to the custodian of enemy property and Indochina which will probably
                        be placed in trust.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>With regard to Bolivian reservation about Metals Reserve contract with
                        International Tin Committee, Campbell stated Committee felt that it had been
                        framed for objectives now unobtainable under circumstances and conditions
                        which have ceased to exist. Committee was therefore willing to approach
                        Embassy to ask it to take up matter with Metals Reserve.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
